[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2716481075","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102937#issuecomment-2716481075","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102937","id":2716481075,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h6jYz","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-12T05:06:58Z","updated_at":"2025-03-12T05:06:58Z","body":"> If we are implementing this new context we should also add it for the following cases which this PR does not implement yet:\r\n> \r\n> * named lambda declarations\r\n\r\nAren't named lambdas just a variable of type `Callable`? I think they work just fine without changes.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f1e3f5de-3876-418e-9cda-5fad14edb553)\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2716481075/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2717989003","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102937#issuecomment-2717989003","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102937","id":2717989003,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iATiL","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-12T14:02:30Z","updated_at":"2025-03-12T14:02:30Z","body":"This should address everything regarding signals, class names and inner classes names, and fixed function implementation. I'm unsure about lambdas though because they seem fine to me.\r\n\r\nI also can't really decide if implementing declaration overlay for enum is worth it or not. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2717989003/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2718302680","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102937#issuecomment-2718302680","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102937","id":2718302680,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iBgHY","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-12T15:37:23Z","updated_at":"2025-03-12T15:37:23Z","body":"> I also can't really decide if implementing declaration overlay for enum is worth it or not.\r\n\r\nI'd say it is (or is there any technical challenge involved?)\r\n\r\n> Aren't named lambdas just a variable of type `Callable`? I think they work just fine without changes.\r\n\r\nThe variable is just a container for the unamed lambda. A named lambda has a name attached to the value (for debugging purposes). It is written like this:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar lambda = func test(): print(\"Hello World\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis isn't really about the hover hint tbh, since it probably wouldn't really show anything useful. But I think it is important to have the context applied consistently to all declarations, since it is used for multiple editor functionalities.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reaction